g Petition |\n| EM-100-INFO* | 9/1/2018 | Emancipation Pamphlet |\n| EM-100-INFO C | 9/1/2018 | Emancipation Pamphlet (Chinese) |\n| EM-100-INFO K | 9/1/2018 | Emancipation Pamphlet (Korean) |\n| EM-100-INFO S | 9/1/2018 | Emancipation Pamphlet (Spanish) |\n| EM-100-INFO V | 9/1/2018 | Emancipation Pamphlet (Vietnamese) |\n| EM-109* | 9/1/2018 | Notice of Hearing—Emancipation of Minor |\n| EM-115* | 9/1/2018 | Emancipation of Minor Income and Expense Declaration |\n| EM-130* | 9/1/2018 | Declaration of Emancipation of Minor After Hearing |\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMemorandum (https://courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-12/102309itema20.pdf)\nciteturn1713search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 17.0 years ago; Crawled: 17.0 years ago; *Attachment to Proof of Electronic Service (Documents Served)* (form POS-050(D)/EFS-050(D)) would make it easy for persons using the *Proof of Electronic Service* form to list additional documents served.\n² It would be optional.\n\n*Attachment to Proof of Electronic Service (Documents Served)* (form POS-050(D)/EFS-050(D)) would make it easy for persons using the *Proof of Electronic Service* form to list additional documents served. *Attachment to Proof of Electronic Service (Persons Served)* (form POS-050(P)/EFS-050(P)) would make it easy for persons using the *Proof of Electronic Service* form to identify additional parties served and indicate the dates and times of service. The attachments would be optional.\n\n*Revision of Current Proof of Service Form*  \nThis proposal recommends the revision of the multipurpose proof of service form, which includes a proof of electronic service. *Proof of Electronic Service—Civil* (form POS-040) would be revised to delete from the end of item 6.f (on electronic service) the following sentence: “I did not receive, within a reasonable time after the transmission, any electronic message or other indication that the transmission was unsuccessful.” This\n\n¹ See *Proof of Service—Civil* (form POS-040).\n\n² The new proof of electronic service form does not include a statement that the “the transmission was reported as complete and without error,” as currently required under rule 2.260(f)(1)(D). The reason is that this language would no longer be required in proofs of electronic service under a proposed amendment to rule 2.260 that is being recommended in a separate rules proposal that is circulating at the same time as this forms proposal.\n\n2--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms/all-by-category)\nciteturn1713search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; # Find Your Court Forms ...   * EFS-050(D) Attachment to Proof of Electronic Service (Documents Served) Effective: January 1, 2010\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * EFS-020 * Proposed Order (Cover Sheet) Effective: February 1, 2017\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * EFS-050 Proof of Electronic Service Effective: February 1, 2017\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * EFS-050(D) Attachment to Proof of Electronic Service (Documents Served) Effective: January 1, 2010\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * EFS-050(P) Attachment to Proof of Electronic Service (Persons Served) Effective: February 1, 2017\n\nSee form info Download\n\n## [Button: Emancipation of Minor]\n\n  * EM-100 * Petition for Declaration of Emancipation of Minor, Order Prescribing Notice, Declaration of Emancipation, and Order Denying Petition Effective: September 1, 2018\n\nSee form info Download\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=0&query=SER-)\nciteturn1713search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; # Find Your Court Forms ...   * EFS-050(D) Attachment to Proof of Electronic Service (Documents Served) Effective: January 1, 2010\nSe